<div class="component container col-12">
    <div class="component-content" >

    <div class="component footnotes col-12">
        <div class="component-content">
<div class="cf-footnotes">
    <h5>Footnotes</h5>
        <ol>
                    <li id="cf-fn-1">Nobu Kiyotaki and John Moore, &ldquo;Credit Cycles,&rdquo; <em>Journal of Political Economy</em> 105, 1997, pp. 211-248.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-1" aria-label="Return from footnote 1.">Return to 1</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-2">Markus K. Brunnermeier and Yuliy Sannikov, &ldquo;A Macroeconomic Model with a Financial Sector,&rdquo; <em>American Economic Review</em> 104, 2014, pp. 379-421.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-2" aria-label="Return from footnote 2.">Return to 2</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-3">See Ivo Krznar and James Morsink, &ldquo;With Great Power Comes Great Responsibility: Macroprudential Tools at Work in Canada,&rdquo; IMF Working Paper WP/14/83, May 2014.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-3" aria-label="Return from footnote 3.">Return to 3</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-4">See Stanley Fischer, &ldquo;Macroprudential Policy in Action: Israel,&rdquo; in George A. Akerlof, Olivier J. Blanchard, David Romer, and Joseph E. Stiglitz, eds., <em>What Have We Learned? Macroeconomic Policy after the Crisis</em> (Cambridge, Mass: The MIT Press), 2014, pp. 87-98.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-4" aria-label="Return from footnote 4.">Return to 4</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-5">See Eliana Balla and Andrew McKenna, &ldquo;Dynamic Provisioning: A Countercyclical Tool for Loan Loss Reserves,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond <em>Economic Quarterly</em>, 95, Fall 2009, pp. 383-418.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-5" aria-label="Return from footnote 5.">Return to 5</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-6">See Stanley Fischer, &ldquo;Financial Sector Reform: How Far Are We?&rdquo; Martin Feldstein Lecture, National Bureau of Economic Research, Cambridge, MA, July 10, 2014.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-6" aria-label="Return from footnote 6.">Return to 6</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-7">See Balla and McKenna, p. 403.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-7" aria-label="Return from footnote 7.">Return to 7</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-8">See C. Lim, F. Columba, A. Costa, P. Kongsamut, A. Otani, M. Saiyid, T. Wezel, and X. Wu, &ldquo;Macroprudential Policy: What Instruments and How to Use Them? Lessons from Country Experiences,&rdquo; IMF Working Paper WP/11/238, October 2011.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-8" aria-label="Return from footnote 8.">Return to 8</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-9">The Cleveland Financial Stress Index is updated daily.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-9" aria-label="Return from footnote 9.">Return to 9</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-10">For an informative discussion of the nature of the models, see Eric M. Leeper and James M. Nason, &ldquo;Bringing Financial Stability into Monetary Policy,&rdquo; November 11, 2014.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-10" aria-label="Return from footnote 10.">Return to 10</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-11">Yves Mersch, member of the Executive Board of the European Central Bank, discusses some of this research in &ldquo;Monetary Policy and Economic Inequality,&rdquo; keynote speech, Corporate Credit Conference, Zurich, October 17, 2014.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-11" aria-label="Return from footnote 11.">Return to 11</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-12">See &ldquo;Developments Related to Financial Stability,&rdquo; in the <em>Monetary Policy Report</em>, Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, July 15, 2014, pp. 22-23.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-12" aria-label="Return from footnote 12.">Return to 12</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-13">Footnote 13
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-13" aria-label="Return from footnote 13.">Return to 13</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-14">See Randall S. Kroszner, &ldquo;What Should Central Banks Do? Comments on Charles Goodhart&rsquo;s &lsquo;The Changing Role of Central Banks,&rsquo;&rdquo; remarks at the BIS Annual Research Conference, Lucerne, June 2010.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-14" aria-label="Return from footnote 14.">Return to 14</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-15">See Frederic S. Mishkin, &ldquo;How Should We Respond to Asset Price Bubbles?,&rdquo; speech at the Wharton Financial Institutions Center and Oliver Wyman Institute&rsquo;s Annual Financial Risk Roundtable, Philadelphia, May 15, 2008.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-15" aria-label="Return from footnote 15.">Return to 15</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-16">See Jordi Gali, &ldquo;Monetary Policy and Rational Asset Price Bubbles,&rdquo; <em>American Economic Review</em> 104, 2014, pp. 721-752.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-16" aria-label="Return from footnote 16.">Return to 16</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-17">See Jeremy C. Stein, &ldquo;Overheating in Credit Markets: Origins, Measurement, and Policy Responses,&rdquo; remarks at &ldquo;Restoring Household Financial Stability after the Great Recession: Why Household Balance Sheets Matter,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis Research Symposium, St. Louis, February 7, 2013.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-17" aria-label="Return from footnote 17.">Return to 17</a>
                    </li>
        </ol>
</div>
